I can see the problem. There are actually multiple issues working together:

**1. `TextMessage` is not memoized at all.**
[TextMessage.tsx:51](src/screens/room/fragments/text-message/TextMessage.tsx#L51) exports a plain `FC`. When `SingleMessageTypeInner` re-renders, `TextMessage` always re-renders with it — no protection.

**2. The `SingleMessageType` comparator has a gap that lets scroll-triggered re-renders through.**
In [SingleMessageType.tsx:125-136](src/screens/room/fragments/single-message-type/SingleMessageType.tsx#L125-L136), when the event key matches but the reference differs (SDK typically gives new object instances after `markAsRead()` fires read receipt updates), it returns `false` → re-renders `SingleMessageTypeInner` → re-renders `TextMessage`.

**3. Several FlashList callbacks are not memoized.**
In [RoomTimeline.tsx:153-178](src/screens/room/fragments/room-timeline/RoomTimeline.tsx#L153-L178), `handleOnScroll`, `handleContentSizeChange`, and `keyExtractor` are recreated on every render. Each scroll tick calls `setShowScrollDown`, which re-renders `RoomTimeline`, giving FlashList new function prop references and causing it to call `renderItem` for visible items.

---

**The chain on scroll:**
`setShowScrollDown` → `RoomTimeline` re-renders → FlashList gets new `onScroll`/`keyExtractor`/`onContentSizeChange` → calls `renderItem` for visible items → `SingleMessageType` comparator: if event ref changed (e.g. from `markAsRead()`) → returns `false` → `TextMessage` re-renders.

**Fixes (in priority order):**

**Fix 1** — Memoize `TextMessage` with the same key-based comparator:

```tsx
export const TextMessage = memo<Props>(
  ({ roomId, event, isPreviousSameSender, onMemberPress }) => {
    // existing body unchanged
  },
  (prev, next) => {
    if (getItemUniqueKey(prev.event) !== getItemUniqueKey(next.event)) return false;
    if (prev.isPreviousSameSender !== next.isPreviousSameSender) return false;
    if (prev.event === next.event) return true;
    return false; // different ref → allow re-render for content/reaction updates
  },
);
```

**Fix 2** — Memoize the FlashList callbacks in `RoomTimeline` to reduce unnecessary re-render cascades:

```tsx
const handleOnScroll = useCallback(({ nativeEvent }: ...) => { ... }, [loadMoreMessages, markAsRead]);
const handleContentSizeChange = useCallback((_w, h) => { ... }, [loadMoreMessages]);
const keyExtractor = useCallback((item) => { ... }, []);
```

Fix 1 is the most impactful because even if `SingleMessageTypeInner` re-renders, `TextMessage` won't unless the event actually changed. Fix 2 reduces how often the cascade starts in the first place.

Want me to apply both?

